 "name": "Bouffalant",
 "notes": [
  "Painted design: one Body_dif shared by two materials: Body (shader 1731682751, no normal sampler; _dif + _par) and BodyB = the afro (flocky shader, normal slot = dummy_flocky_texture, no _par slot). Afro (island 26) painted as dark soft cloudy clumps; brown body fur with visible radial strokes; grey lower legs and grey muzzle with fine strokes and one dark mouth line; cream horns with painted darker growth bands; orange horn rings; grey hooves.",
  "So: afro = dense curly fur whose short curved strands wrap the painted clumps (curls treatment, species_ext_curls.py); body = short fur along the painted strokes; lower legs and muzzle shorter; horns = smooth keratin with soft grooves only on the painted bands; hooves = painted grain only; rings, mouth, teeth, nose and the small bits untouched.",
  "Island ids come from both materials (mat Body|BodyB, species_author_ext.py).",
  "Round 2 (11-14): the afro is the species' signature (a huge springy mass of curled wool that cushions its headbutts), and round 1 curls (2-3 texels) vanished in game. Now two layers (stack): the painted cloud clumps at a 12-texel scale with deep soft gaps (curls, form-dominated) for mid range, plus short tightly bent locks (fur_locks, curl 2.6 rad, 13 texels long) for close range, so the afro reads as piled coiled wool. Body and lower legs: straight short locks along the painted strokes. In game the afro's normal slot (BodyB, flocky shader) is repointed from dummy_flocky_texture to Body_nor (matinstb_repoint.py) and the Body material is twin-swapped, so both show the normal; bake_ao lowered to 0.12 because the real normal now carries the relief."
 ],
